<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Friuli</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Friuli is a historical region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, the Adriatic and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soca">Isonzo</a>, now part of Friuli-Venezia Giulia. It takes its name from the Roman town of Forum Iulii, modern Cividale. It was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> duchy and a Carolingian march, then largely ruled by the Patriarchate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aquileia">Aquileia</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> conquered it in 1420.</p></div>
